# ============================================================================
# Databricks Module - Outputs
# ============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE:
#   This file defines output values that the module exposes to the calling
#   module. Outputs allow the root module to access information about resources
#   created within this module.
#
# KEY CONCEPTS FOR BEGINNERS:
#   - Module outputs: Values exposed from the module to the caller
#   - Accessing outputs: Root modules use module.<name>.<output> syntax
#   - Output dependencies: Outputs can reference any resource created in the module
#   - Information hiding: Only outputs are accessible outside the module
#
# TERRAFORM DOCUMENTATION:
#   - Module Outputs: https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/modules/develop/outputs
#   - Accessing Module Outputs: https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/modules/syntax#accessing-module-output-values
#
# USAGE EXAMPLE:
#   In the root module, you would access outputs like:
#   output "workspace_url" {
#     value = module.databricks.workspace_url
#   }
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WORKSPACE OUTPUTS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The URL to access the Databricks workspace
# This is the web address users will use to log into Databricks
# Format varies by provider:
#   - AWS: https://<workspace-id>.cloud.databricks.com
#   - Azure: https://adb-<workspace-id>.<region>.azuredatabricks.net
#   - GCP: https://<workspace-id>.gcp.databricks.com
output "workspace_url" {
  description = "Databricks workspace URL - use this to access the workspace in a web browser"
  value       = "Configured in main.tf"
  
  # Note: In a complete implementation, this would reference the actual workspace resource:
  # value = databricks_mws_workspaces.this.workspace_url
  # or
  # value = azurerm_databricks_workspace.this.workspace_url
  #
  # This output is useful for:
  # - Root modules that need to pass the URL to other modules
  # - Displaying the URL after deployment
  # - Configuring CI/CD pipelines
  # - Documentation and sharing with team members
}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: Additional Outputs
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In a complete module implementation, you would also have outputs for:
# - workspace_id: Unique identifier for the workspace
# - workspace_name: Name of the workspace (for reference)
# - deployment_name: Deployment identifier
# - network_id: Network configuration ID (if applicable)
# - storage_configuration_id: Storage configuration ID (if applicable)
# - credentials_id: Credentials configuration ID (if applicable)
